  "purpose": "controlled response probe for traversability: measure, per 4 px cell and per bearing, whether a declared press actually moves the hero. The incidental grid this replaces was aggregated from transitions the planner produced while it was already failing, so its samples are biased towards the cells and directions the planner preferred - at the cell where the v14 stage died, north carried 125 samples and north was the ineffective direction. This probe declares an opposite-pairs schedule so each direction is immediately answered by its opposite and the hero stays in a small cluster of cells instead of random-walking away, and it interleaves idle control windows so a press is compared against the drift the hero would have had anyway. The analyser emits the same frozen grid shape the Router mask already consumes, drift-subtracted and at a declared press duration.",
